  "text_md": "Using the formula just proved,\n\n$$\nd cos u = sin U du.\n$$\n\n38. Proof of IX, X, XI, and XII. Differentiating both sides of the equation sin u\n\n$$\ntan u COS U\n$$\n\nand using\n\n$$\ncoS u d sin u sin u d cos u cos? u du + sin? u du d tan u U Cos? u cos?\n$$\n\n$$\nsec? u du.\n$$\n\nsec du. By differentiating both sides of the equations\n\n$$\ncot u sec U = CSC U\n$$\n\n$$\nsin U\n$$\n\nand using the formulas for the differentials of sin u and cos u t we obtain the differentials of cot u, sec u and esc u.\n\nExample 1. y = sin 2 (x 2 + 3).\n\nSince\n\n$$\nsin? (x? + 3) = [sin (x? + 3)],\n$$\n\nwe use the formula for u 2 and so get\n\n$$\ndy = 2 sin (x2 + 3) d sin (x? + 3) 4 2 sin (x2 + 3) cos (x2 + 3) dz.\n$$\n\nEx. 2.\n\n$$\ndy d sec 2 2 sec 2 2 dc dz dx\n$$\n\n# EXERCISES\n\nIn the following exorcises show that the derivatives and differentials have the values given:\n\nhave the values given:\n\n$$\ny = 2sin 3 z + 3 cos dy (cos 3 r dc 2 5,\n$$\n\n",
